      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Korogocho"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The slum began in the 1960s when rural migrants settled on vacant government land, forming a shanty town on Nairobi’s outskirts.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Korogocho"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Korogocho sits directly beside Nairobi’s largest rubbish dump, Dandora, a fact that shapes its environmental challenges.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Korogocho"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Despite its density, many residents keep small plots of land for farming, turning narrow streets into miniature gardens.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
